Discussion: OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353

From our per-feature patches `13-dwarf-multicannon` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), applied with `git am` on `main` (`1be5dfb5f`); commits kept as they are except for the `feat:`/`fix:` subject.

**Problem.** The dwarf multicannon could not be set up.

**Change.** New module `content/other/dwarf-multicannon`:
- Set-up in four stages, loading, firing, pick-up and decay, with the OSRS varps client plugins read (`dropcannon` stage, `rockthrower` ammo, `ownedmcannon` coord, `mcannon_decayed`).
- A cannon left behind by a logout, or one that decays, goes back to the owner's bank.
- Timers `mcannon_fire` (440) and `mcannon_decay` (441).

**Tests.** `DwarfMulticannonTest` (7, integration).

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`; `assemble`, `test` and `integration` as separate runs in a 4 GB container): cache build pass, `spotlessCheck` pass, `assemble test integration` pass, boot: Server ready in 6.952898445s.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; in-game checks mentioned above were on our own server build (main's pin `9a8b338a8` plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** Varps and locs from the cache; varp meanings as RuneLite's Cannon plugin reads them (BSD).

**Caveats.**
- Timer ids 440/441 are our choice (see question 3 in #353).

**Release note.** The dwarf multicannon can be set up, loaded, fired and picked up.

